{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpnVkRGFUNSob7b39s72","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"In Vitest 5, `vitest list` reads each test file's source and parses it into an AST (syntax tree) instead of importing and running it. It then walks that tree for `describe`, `test` and `it` calls, plus forms like `test.describe` and their modifiers, and builds the list of suites and tests from those calls. The v5.0.0 release notes list this as a breaking change (\"Parse files statically in vitest list by default\", #11088). The same release moved the underlying `parseSpecifications` API out of experimental and shares the AST collection code with typechecking.\n\nBecause nothing runs, setup files, imports and side effects never execute, so listing is faster. The catch is that tests created at runtime can't be fully resolved this way. That includes tests made in loops, names computed from variables, and calls through computed members like `test[mode](...)`, which static collection ignores. The release notes don't say how to switch back to the old run-to-collect behavior, so check `vitest list --help` if you need it.\n\nSources:\n- [Vitest v5.0.0 release notes](https://github.com/vitest-dev/vitest/releases/tag/v5.0.0)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":580,"cache_read_input_tokens":5383,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":580},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ad210a8-7382-46a1-a195-fbfa1c412077","uuid":"bd967414-30a1-4d17-809f-4548afbb9ad7","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:40:04.286Z","request_id":"req_011CfpnVk4RpRk7MnHCMMT6L"}
